## 2. Attack summary

Rocky-family systems (RHEL/CentOS/Rocky) are the enterprise Linux most often seen in the field, which is why this endpoint uses `/var/log/secure`, `auditd`, and `firewalld` rather than a Debian-style layout.

| # | Technique | ATT&CK | Data source | Detection |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Brute Force (SSH) | T1110 | `/var/log/secure` | Built-in — two-level (single + aggregate) |
| 2 | Scheduled Task/Job (cron) | T1053.003 | auditd / cron log | Built-in — "Crontab entry changed" |
| 3 | Command & Scripting (Unix Shell) | T1059.004 | auditd `execve` | **Custom rule 100200** |

